    {
        "id": "2-2",
        "text": "- **Continual Popularity \u2013 No chance of Linux as a whole going out of business, as it is not**\nowned by any one company. Linux has been growing on the server and desktop market\nexponentially since the early 1990s.\n\n  - Did we mention that Open Source software is generally FREE in cost?\n\nThis means that software can be of high quality for everyone, and money can be made out of\nsupport, distribution, training or working with open source software.\nIt\u2019s a revolutionary change in the way we perceive software and do business, however huge names\nlike IBM, HP and Intel and even non IT firms such as Boeing, Glaxo Smithkline and thousands more\nare all using Open Source and Linux. Some of them are even putting work back into it.\n\n\n-----",
